[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known: one issue, one fix queued. The reports said otherwise.
They were merged by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and every
subject says "wrong day". Behind that subject sat two different bugs, each with its own ticket.
Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October: the parser is fixed, the hint is won't fix.

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  tickets={{
    parser: 'https://github.com/spyrad/mega-what-it-shows/issues/1',
    hint: 'https://github.com/spyrad/mega-what-it-shows/issues/2'
  }}
/>

## The two problems

- **`parser`:** the shared parser reads every date month first. Our tenants write the day first,
  so "7 April" becomes "4 July". App, email, and the `booking-v2` form, whose hint asks for the
  day first.
- **`hint`:** the `booking-v3` form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type the month
  first, as told, and the form reads the day first. Same symptom, different code: only the three
  tenants on `booking-v3`, only through the form.

<Callout kind="warn">
Do not count by intake tag. <code>intakeTag</code> is guessed from the reporter's browser and
disagrees with the cause in dozens of reports. The cause comes from the tenant and the channel
(<code>causes.ts</code>).
</Callout>

## What changes for the desk

- `parser` ([#1](https://github.com/spyrad/mega-what-it-shows/issues/1)): fixed — `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
- `hint` ([#2](https://github.com/spyrad/mega-what-it-shows/issues/2)): won't fix — the `booking-v3` form is retired.
- "Known" was true for one of two.
- Merging on subject alone hides causes that share a symptom. Before marking a big ticket known,
  split it by cause with this table.
- The one-day moves in the footnote may be a third bug (time zones). Check whether they still
  come in now that the parser fix is out.

